WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.331
Since President Trump
took office there's been

00:00:02.331 --> 00:00:05.103
a lot of rhetoric about building a wall

00:00:05.103 --> 00:00:07.242
along the Mexican border and imposing

00:00:07.242 --> 00:00:09.690
a high tariff on Mexican goods.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.154
Well, I was thinking I
wanted to take things

00:00:12.154 --> 00:00:14.514
in a more positive direction, after all,

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.378
the beautiful thing about television

00:00:16.378 --> 00:00:18.932
is there are no walls, no such thing.

00:00:18.932 --> 00:00:20.975
So ladies and gentlemen, here's the plan,

00:00:20.975 --> 00:00:23.517
I'm going to go down to Mexico City,

00:00:23.517 --> 00:00:26.712
rent a television studio
and shoot an episode

00:00:26.712 --> 00:00:29.966
of our show with the help
of an all Mexican staff,

00:00:29.966 --> 00:00:32.818
crew, guests, and studio audience.

00:00:32.818 --> 00:00:37.385
We're calling it Conan Without
Borders Made in Mexico.

00:00:37.385 --> 00:00:40.218
(audience cheers)

00:00:43.866 --> 00:00:45.695
I think it's gonna be fun.

00:00:45.695 --> 00:00:46.641
No, no.

00:00:46.641 --> 00:00:48.227
No border can contain the nonsense

00:00:48.227 --> 00:00:50.438
that we perform on this show.
Yes.

00:00:50.438 --> 00:00:53.727
The uselessness, the time that we waste.

00:00:53.727 --> 00:00:57.011
Our idiocy must be shared
throughout the world.

00:00:57.011 --> 00:01:00.656
Well, to get people in Mexico
excited about our show,

00:01:00.656 --> 00:01:03.639
here's what we're doing,
we're posting this version

00:01:03.639 --> 00:01:07.710
of last night's monologue
on our Team Coco website

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.722
so that everyone can get
used to my comedic stylings

00:01:10.722 --> 00:01:12.988
south of the border, take a look.

00:01:12.988 --> 00:01:15.469
Starbucks siempre ha sido un sitio

00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:19.666
para gente que no tiene
no otro lugar donde estar.

00:01:19.666 --> 00:01:21.768
(audience laughing)

00:01:21.768 --> 00:01:23.768
Se entre, con su laptop.

00:01:25.166 --> 00:01:27.462
Hay gente que han estado alli nueve anos

00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:29.504
escribiendo un solo guion.

00:01:29.504 --> 00:01:31.567
El mismo guion.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:33.014
Todos estan trabajando

00:01:33.014 --> 00:01:34.503
en el mismo guion.

00:01:34.503 --> 00:01:36.808
(woman laughs)

00:01:36.808 --> 00:01:39.808
(audience applauds)

00:01:43.313 --> 00:01:46.132
I don't know why
you're a Japanese woman,

00:01:46.132 --> 00:01:48.207
but we'll figure it out.

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:49.855
I'm just always touched
when someone understands

00:01:49.855 --> 00:01:51.306
what I'm trying to do.

00:01:51.306 --> 00:01:55.473
Again, that's Conan Without
Borders, Made in Mexico.

00:01:57.136 --> 00:02:00.082
Our goal is to make a lot of friends.

00:02:00.082 --> 00:02:03.149
It's airing Wednesday, March 1st at 10 pm,

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:06.039
right here on TBS, so watch for that.

00:02:06.039 --> 00:02:09.220
We'll be right back.
(audience cheers)

